  "planning_notes": [
    "Board fixed to arduino:avr:uno. Pins preserved per authoritative wiring: Button D2; LEDs D10 (green) and D13 (red); buzzer D6; ultrasonic entrance Trig D8 Echo D9; ultrasonic parking Trig D11 Echo D12; TM1637 CLK D4 DIO D5.",
    "No explicit serial protocol/baud/commands/report cadence was provided; therefore no serial_channels are declared.",
    "Ultrasonic timeout_us chosen as 30000 within 25000..60000 range. Actual sample_period_ms must be rounded up to a control-period multiple by the implementation with minimum >= ceil((timeout_us+12)/1000) and >=60ms; acquisition invalid_policy is hold_last_valid for both distance and validity.",
    "Button wiring polarity (active-high vs active-low) and pullup usage were not specified. Catalog digital_input defaults are used (unspecified pull configuration uses legal catalog default).",
    "TM1637 number digit layout, number of wired digits (1..4), and segment register mapping are not provided in the prompt; however the requirement only states CLK/DIO pins and that the display shows distance/occupancy. Since shift register mapping is not provided and tm1637_number does not require segment wiring, this is treated as a generic TM1637 module compatible with the catalog driver."
